---
import { PUBLIC_APP_NAME, PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL } from "astro:env/client";
---

<section id="faq" class="py-16 relative overflow-hidden border-t border-slate-800">
  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
    <div class="text-center space-y-6 mb-12">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 bg-slate-800/50 backdrop-blur-sm border border-slate-700 rounded-full px-6 py-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-cyan-400 rounded-full animate-pulse"></span>
        <span class="text-slate-300 font-medium">FAQ</span>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-white">
        Frequently Asked <span class="gradient-text">Questions</span>
      </h2>

      <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Answers to common questions about our browser-based speech-to-text dictation app.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <details class="group border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-6 bg-slate-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">What browsers does {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} support?</h3>
          <span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">⌄</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">{PUBLIC_APP_NAME} works best in Google Chrome and also supports Safari. It runs directly in your browser, with no downloads or extensions required.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-6 bg-slate-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Is {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} free?</h3>
          <span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">⌄</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">Yes. {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} is free as in beer 🍺 You can optionally bring your own API keys to use premium speech models.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-6 bg-slate-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Which devices and platforms are supported?</h3>
          <span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">⌄</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">{PUBLIC_APP_NAME} is cross‑platform: Windows, macOS, Linux, iPhone, iPad, and Android. If your device has a modern browser and microphone, you're good to go.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-6 bg-slate-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">How accurate is it? Do you store my audio?</h3>
          <span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">⌄</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">Accuracy is around 99.5%, but depends on your microphone and speech. Speak clearly; like how a newscaster reads the news. Your browser sends your speech to Google, Apple, Microsoft, or Assembly AI to do the speech-to-text, similar to dictating a text message on your phone; see the <a href={PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL} class="text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-300 transition-colors duration-200">Privacy Policy</a> for details on data handling.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="group border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-6 bg-slate-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Can I use my own API keys?</h3>
          <span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">⌄</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">Yes. Bring your own keys to unlock premium speech recognition models while keeping full control over your usage and costs.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQPage JSON-LD -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "What browsers does Tater Talk support?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Tater Talk works best in Google Chrome and also supports Safari. It runs directly in your browser. No downloads or extensions required." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Is Tater Talk free?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Yes. Tater Talk is free as in beer. You can optionally bring your own API keys to use premium speech models." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Which devices and platforms are supported?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Tater Talk is cross‑platform: Windows, macOS, Linux, iPhone, iPad, and Android. If your device has a modern browser and microphone, you're good to go." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "How accurate is it? Do you store my audio?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Accuracy is around 99.5%, but depends on your microphone and speech. Speak clearly; like how a newscaster reads the news. Your browser sends your speech to Google, Apple, Microsoft, or Assembly AI to do the speech-to-text, similar to dictating a text message on your phone; see the Privacy Policy for details on data handling." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Can I use my own API keys?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Yes. Bring your own keys to unlock premium speech recognition models while keeping full control over your usage and costs." }
      }
    ]
  })}>
  </script>
</section>


